#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/fp8/index.rst:2
msgid "tilelang.contrib.cutedsl.fp8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/fp8/index.rst:8
msgid "FP8 (e4m3 / e5m2) elementwise arithmetic for the CuTeDSL backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/fp8/index.rst:10
msgid ""
"No PTX instruction computes on e4m3/e5m2 registers on sm_89/sm_90/sm_120, "
"and CuTeDSL cannot lower ``arith`` ops on FP8 MLIR types. Each operation is "
"therefore one inline PTX block on packed registers: widen with "
"``cvt.rn.f16x2.{e4m3x2,e5m2x2}``, compute in ``f16x2``, and narrow with "
"``cvt.rn.satfinite``. Every FP8 value is exact in f16, and f16 carries more "
"than ``2p + 2`` significand bits for both formats, so rounding the f16 "
"result once more to FP8 gives the correctly rounded FP8 result. Division has "
"no f16 instruction and multiplies by ``rcp.approx.ftz.f32`` (relative error "
"about 2^-22; FP8 magnitudes never reach f32 subnormals): a quotient of two "
"FP8 values that is not exactly an FP8 rounding midpoint lies at least about "
"2^-9 (relative) away from one, so the approximation still rounds to the "
"correctly rounded FP8 quotient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/fp8/index.rst:22
msgid ""
"``max``/``min`` use the ``.NaN`` forms (NaN propagates, ``+0 > -0``), "
"matching the ``arith.maximumf``/``minimumf`` semantics CuTeDSL uses for "
"other float types."
msgstr ""

